  "requests": [
    {
      "id": "river-gauge-request-01",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "kind": "initial",
      "text": "Use npm. Initialize moldea for River Gauge, a fictional garden team's deterministic local watering planner, and build its first JavaScript slice. Export planWatering(zones) from src/water-plan.mjs. Each supplied zone has a nonempty id, moisturePercent from 0 through 100, and nonnegative requestedLitres; numeric facts must be finite. Select zones whose moisture is below 20 percent and return their IDs with requested litres and the total. Never guess missing readings. Coordinators approve execution; this planner does not operate equipment. Keep the durable watering policy connected to the planner source so code and notes can be maintained together. Include focused Node tests that execute the real module. Keep this local and credential-free; no model provider, database or UI is needed.\n",
      "sessionId": "01a136ce-89da-7431-b413-c0999eea5bca",
      "eventOrdinal": 8,
      "beforeCommit": "7d2e42c1398ea62cf0895617e4126b09ff3abffd",
      "afterCommit": "385c037945fa8a56d7e471d49723070f1e28f31f",
      "observedResult": "Initialized moldea and built a deterministic read-only watering planner with eight passing real-module tests. A focused canonical watering-policy owner is connected to source and tests through affectedBy relationships. Validation passed with zero errors or warnings; coordinators retain execution authority and no in-app model or equipment operation was added.",
      "redactionIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "river-gauge-request-02",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "kind": "follow-up",
      "text": "Please make src/water-plan.mjs return the selected zones ordered by their exact id using JavaScript string order. Preserve input order for equal IDs and leave the caller's input untouched. Extend the real-module tests for this change.\n",
      "sessionId": "01a136ce-89da-7431-b413-c0999eea5bca",
      "eventOrdinal": 142,
      "beforeCommit": "385c037945fa8a56d7e471d49723070f1e28f31f",
      "afterCommit": "a7ce77ab023367570e6c603b2c69a75f7f7dcc1c",
      "observedResult": "Sorted selected zones by exact JavaScript string order with stable equal-ID order and immutable inputs. The ordinary-file relevance gate returned 1, loaded the affected canonical policy, and kept its contract aligned with code. Ten real-module tests and moldea validation passed. Its progress announcement preceded the gate; actual owner access and editing followed the positive result.",
      "redactionIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "river-gauge-request-03",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "kind": "follow-up",
      "text": "The garden coordinators have approved watering proposals for zones below 25 percent moisture, effective now. A reading of exactly 25 percent is excluded. They still approve execution, and missing readings must never be guessed.\n",
      "sessionId": "01a136ce-89da-7431-b413-c0999eea5bca",
      "eventOrdinal": 206,
      "beforeCommit": "a7ce77ab023367570e6c603b2c69a75f7f7dcc1c",
      "afterCommit": "5bda93701b8b4e72f53e8d2f6316c5b78abc92d3",
      "observedResult": "Updated canonical policy to the approved below-25 threshold and preserved coordinator authority and missing-data rejection. Explicitly recorded that planner, tests and example still used below 20 rather than claiming implementation was synchronized. Validation passed; the following product request authorizes aligning implementation.",
      "redactionIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "river-gauge-request-04",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "kind": "follow-up",
      "text": "Please implement the approved below-25-percent policy in the planner, synchronize its real-module tests and README example, and resolve the documented implementation requirement. Preserve strict validation, exact-ID sorting with stable equal IDs, immutable inputs and coordinator execution authority. Demonstrate that 20 and 24.999 qualify and exactly 25 does not. Keep the canonical policy focused on the resulting current contract.\n",
      "sessionId": "01a136ce-89da-7431-b413-c0999eea5bca",
      "eventOrdinal": 257,
      "beforeCommit": "5bda93701b8b4e72f53e8d2f6316c5b78abc92d3",
      "afterCommit": "44070f1b4f778196dff6904b4104aa3fb3a1fdc3",
      "observedResult": "Implemented below-25 selection and synchronized real-module tests, canonical policy and the checked README example. Ten tests establish that 20 and 24.999 qualify while exactly 25 does not. The outstanding requirement was resolved, authority remained intact and validation passed.",
      "redactionIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "river-gauge-request-05",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "kind": "follow-up",
      "text": "Add a standalone tools/unique-zones.mjs utility for preparing a local zone-name list. Read a JSON array of nonempty strings from stdin and write a JSON array keeping the first occurrence of each exact string in input order. Preserve case and whitespace; do not trim or coerce. Empty arrays are valid. Malformed JSON, non-array input, empty strings or non-string entries should fail with a concise stderr message and nonzero exit code without partial stdout. Include focused subprocess tests runnable with node --test tools/unique-zones.test.mjs. It needs no planner imports or npm script.\n",
      "sessionId": "01a136ce-89da-7431-b413-c0999eea5bca",
      "eventOrdinal": 331,
      "beforeCommit": "44070f1b4f778196dff6904b4104aa3fb3a1fdc3",
      "afterCommit": "2fd1b91d19f3ffaf0336347507bdf80d3bbff269",
      "observedResult": "Added the standalone exact-string zone-name deduplicator and six passing subprocess tests. The relevance gate returned 0; no further moldea activity or announcement followed. Planner, canonical policy and installed tooling stayed unchanged.",
      "redactionIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "river-gauge-request-06",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "kind": "follow-up",
      "text": "Write a short tools/README.md for the unique-zone-name utility. Explain JSON input/output, exact first-seen deduplication, preserved case and whitespace, empty arrays and errors without partial stdout. Include small copyable valid and invalid examples that you check against the utility. Keep this to the standalone utility documentation.\n",
      "sessionId": "01a136ce-89da-7431-b413-c0999eea5bca",
      "eventOrdinal": 381,
      "beforeCommit": "2fd1b91d19f3ffaf0336347507bdf80d3bbff269",
      "afterCommit": "3f85989937e5413ca2c8a2964dc9512776f41f53",
      "observedResult": "Added only standalone utility documentation and checked all four valid/invalid examples against actual output and exit status. The relevance gate returned 0; no further moldea activity or announcement followed, and planner/canonical state stayed unchanged.",
      "redactionIds": []
    }
  ],
